{"name":"Banana Republic","hex":"#ffe292","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"banana republic","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small country, especially one in Central America or the West Indies, that is dependent on a single export commodity (traditionally bananas) and that has a corrupt, dictatorial government."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/banana_republic"}],"entries":[{"title":"Banana Republic","blocks":[{"text":"Banana Republic is an American upscale clothing and accessories retailer owned by The Gap. It was founded in 1978 by Mel and Patricia Ziegler, who named the company \"Banana Republic Travel & Safari Clothing Company\". In 1983, Gap purchased the company, shortened its name to \"Banana Republic\", and rebranded the stores to achieve a more upscale image."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Banana_Republic_%2854076909886%29.jpg/330px-Banana_Republic_%2854076909886%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Banana_Republic","wikidata":"Q806085"},{"title":"Banana republic","blocks":[{"text":"In political science, the term banana republic describes a politically and economically unstable country with an economy dependent upon the export of natural resources."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/William_Sydney_Porter_by_doubleday.jpg/330px-William_Sydney_Porter_by_doubleday.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Banana_republic","wikidata":"Q171751"},{"title":"Banana","blocks":[{"text":"A banana is an elongated, edible fruit that is botanically a berry produced by several kinds of large treelike herbaceous flowering plants in the genus Musa. In some countries, cooking bananas are called plantains, distinguishing them from dessert bananas. The fruit is variable in size, color and firmness, but is usually elongated and curved, with soft flesh rich in starch covered with a peel, which may have a variety of colors when ripe. It grows upward in clusters near the top of the plant. Almost all modern edible seedless (parthenocarp) cultivated bananas come from two wild species – Musa acuminata and Musa balbisiana, or their hybrids."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Bananavarieties.jpg/330px-Bananavarieties.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Banana","wikidata":"Q503"},{"title":"Republic","blocks":[{"text":"A republic, based on the Latin phrase res publica, is a state in which political power rests with the public (people), typically through their representatives—in contrast to an absolute monarchy or a direct democracy. Although a republic is most often a single sovereign state, subnational state entities that have governments that are republican in nature may be referred to as republics."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Republic","wikidata":"Q7270"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Spring1988_BR_Catalog.jpg/500px-Spring1988_BR_Catalog.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Spring1988_BR_Catalog.jpg/1280px-Spring1988_BR_Catalog.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Spring1988_BR_Catalog.jpg/500px-Spring1988_BR_Catalog.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Banana Republic Travel Clothing Catalog No. 35, Spring 1988","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASpring1988_BR_Catalog.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Banana_Republic%2C_107_E_42nd_St%2C_New_York%2C_NY_10017%2C_USA_-_Mar_2013.jpg/500px-Banana_Republic%2C_107_E_42nd_St%2C